    proSe: 'Commonly filed without a lawyer - in Texas justice court practice this sworn statement of inability is the standard path for tenants who cannot post a bond.',
    gotchas: ['Eviction appeal deadlines are among the shortest in the law - 5 days from judgment in Texas justice courts, and similarly short in many states. Count the judgment date today.', 'The landlord can contest the affidavit of inability, and a short hearing follows where you must prove your finances. Bring documentation - pay records, benefit letters, bank statements.', 'During the appeal, rent must go into the court registry on time - in Texas, within the first portion of the appeal period and then monthly. One missed registry payment can result in a writ even while the appeal is pending.'],
